        {
          "id": "Ballot Issue 2B",
          "title": "Orchard Mesa Pool sales and use tax increase and debt",
          "summary": "Raises the City of Grand Junction sales and use tax rate from 3.39% to 3.46% starting January 1, 2027, raising about $1,900,000 in 2027, to repair, renovate and equip the Orchard Mesa swimming pool without expanding it beyond its existing six-lane configuration. It also lets the city take on up to $12,000,000 in debt with a total repayment cost of up to $19,000,000 for the pool work. When the debt is paid off (no later than December 31, 2047), the rate drops by 0.04%, and the remaining 0.03% continues to pay for operating and maintaining the pool.",
          "yesMeans": "Grand Junction raises its sales and use tax to 3.46% and may borrow up to $12,000,000 to renovate the Orchard Mesa pool.",
          "noMeans": "The sales and use tax increase and the pool debt are not approved.",
